SUMMARY:Pre-Event Picnic - Olivette Riverside Concert  
DESCRIPTION:AVL Digital Nomads\n*With warmer weather upon us\, what could 
 be better than a Sunday afternoon of connecting\, socializing\, and listen
 ing to great music with fellow Nomads at an outdoor concert by the beautif
 ul French Broad River?*\n\n**What:** Pre-Concert Social\n**Where:** The La
 wn - Olivette Riverside Pavilion\n**Artists:** Caleb Caudle & the Sweet Cr
 itters\n**When:** 3pm on Sunday\, May 31st\n**To Bring:** BYOB & BYOC (cha
 ir) + Sharable Snacks\n\n**Details**\nJoin fellow music-loving Nomads for 
 a pre-concert picnic on the lawn by the Olivette Riverside Pavilion. Use *
 *[this link](https://www.chatthillsmusic.com/caleb-caudle)** to purchase t
 ickets for **Caleb Caudle & the Sweet Critters** on Sunday\, May 31st. Nom
 ads attending the pre-concert gathering are invited to bring shareable sna
 cks and appetizers\, along with your beverages of choice.\n\nThis informal
  Nomads gathering starts at 3pm. Live music from Caleb Caudle & the Sweet 
 Critters will be from 4 - 6pm.\n\n**What to Bring**\nBring comfortable fol
 ding chairs and/or blankets for picnicking on the lawn. If you want to sit
  in the covered Pavilion for the concert\, you will need your own chair.\n
 \n**The Music**\nNo stranger to Asheville\, **Caleb Caudle & the Sweet Cri
 tters** will be featured at Chatt Hills' 4th "**[Sundays by the River](htt
 ps://www.chatthillsmusic.com/all-shows)**" concert series for 2026. Rooted
  in the North Carolina foothills and refined on stages across the world\, 
 Nashville-based **[Caleb Caudle](https://www.calebcaudle.com/)** delivers 
 the kind of music that stays with you — soulful\, honest\, and impossibl
 e to put in a box. His sound weaves country tradition and indie spirit int
 o something that feels both timeless and alive\, drawing praise from the N
 ew York Times\, Rolling Stone\, and NPR\, and earning him a spot on the ha
 llowed stage of the Grand Ole Opry. Caudle's music is featured on Rolling 
 Stone’s “10 New Country Artists You Need To Know” and “The 10 Best
  Country and Americana Songs To Hear Now” along with NPR’s “Songs We
  Love”. Whether you know him from Merlefest\, Stagecoach\, Kerrville or 
 Sirius XM’s Outlaw Country\, seeing Caudle live is a reminder of why mus
 ic matters — raw storytelling\, real emotion\, and a voice that cuts str
 aight through. Caudle's latest album\, the 10-track "Heavy Thrill\," is se
 t for release on June 5. Come hear Caleb and the band for a riverside trea
 t!\n\n**Tickets**\nWe highly recommend purchasing your tickets in advance.
  Tickets are $25 each ($30.52\, including fees) -- and kids are free! Well
 -behaved dogs are also welcome.\n\n**[Tickets and more info](https://www.c
 hatthillsmusic.com/caleb-caudle)**.\n\n**Directions**\nOlivette is just 15
  minutes from downtown Asheville. Click **[this link](https://maps.app.goo
 .gl/rnqGwUiLLJghxo1r8)** to get directions directly to the parking area fo
 r the Pavilion. Otherwise\, use the address below to get to Olivette and f
 ollow the Chatt Hills event signs to the Pavilion.\nCarpooling is encourag
 ed.\n\n**Chatt Hills Music**\nChatt Hills Music is an independent non-prof
 it organization dedicated to enriching communities through the power of li
 ve music. Chatt Hills brings an eclectic lineup of award-winning artists t
 o Asheville and the surrounding region. From Americana and singer-songwrit
 ers to jazz\, rock\, and classical\, every concert offers a unique musical
  experience.\nThis outdoor concert series takes place just minutes from do
 wntown Asheville at the scenic Olivette Riverside Pavilion\, located along
  the banks of the French Broad River—where great music meets beautiful v
 iews. World-class music\, scenic views\, affordable tickets — and kids a
 re always free.\n\n**The Venue**\nOlivette is a 411-acre planned community
  and historic farm\, located along the French Broad River\, just 6.7 miles
  from downtown Asheville. An agrihood community\, Olivette is home to a vi
 brant vegetable\, fruit and flower farm. With 1.3 miles of river frontage\
 , the community has a seven acre riverfront park with a pavilion\, miles o
 f walking trails\, community gardens\, a dog park\, and multiple neighborh
 ood gathering spaces.
